{
  "version": "example-1",
  "purpose": "Weighted role terms that rank job ads before any model reads them. Build yours from your own profile, never from job ads you have already judged. THIS IS A SYNTHETIC EXAMPLE for the fictional candidate in matcher_profile.example.json.",
  "matching": "Terms are folded (lowercase, diacritics removed) and matched against the ad's title plus description. Each term counts once per ad. A space at the start or end of a term means a word boundary on that side, and every term of four characters or fewer gets boundaries on both sides, so ' rag ' cannot match inside 'uppdrag'. A longer phrase deliberately adds to a shorter term it contains.",
  "weights": "3 = core, evidence-backed fit. 2 = strong adjacent fit. 1 = weak or boilerplate-prone signal. Negative = a profession the candidate cannot do; keep these mild, because an IT role inside a hospital or school still mentions those words.",
